{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1479","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1479","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1479\",\"parent_revision\":\"75934584066501b383d1778a93031b20a8a6fe80\",\"root_revision\":\"887117262756a93fbf5675d8edd4bbcb33abe9aa88ec2390b6e10a59876afdc8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_claim` records no agent identity when a task is claimed. If the claiming agent crashes, the task remains `in-progress` indefinitely with no way to detect abandonment or identify which agent holds it.\\n\\n**Confirmed gap in `sam_schema/core/query.py` lines 464\u2013489:** `claim_task` sets only `task.started` timestamp. `Task.agent` field (model line 123) and `Task.last_activity` field (model lines 143\u2013147) **already exist** in the model but are never written by the claim path.\\n\\n**Confirmed gap in `sam_schema/server.py` lines 586\u2013614:** `sam_claim` MCP tool has no `agent_id` parameter.\\n\\nThis is a **completion gap** \u2014 the data model already supports identity tracking. The write path and MCP API surface do not expose it.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail \u2014 identity and activity tracking fields exist in the model but are not populated  \\n**Pattern**: single-agent assumption exposed by multi-agent swarm usage (kage-bunshin, swarm dispatch)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 `claim_task` function (lines 464\u2013489)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `sam_claim` tool (lines 586\u2013614)\\n\\n**Verify only (no change needed):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Task.agent` (line 123) and `Task.last_activity` (lines 143\u2013147) confirmed present\\n\\n**Tests (new):**\\n- `tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 agent_id claim recording tests\\n- `tests_sam/test_cli_claim.py` \u2014 CLI claim with agent_id\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 calls `sam_claim` without passing identity; canonical dispatch pattern\\n- `skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 documents `sam_claim` as first step for every task agent\\n- `skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` and `scripts/health.py` \u2014 health monitoring cannot correlate back to SAM task ownership\\n- `skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 initiates claim; no recovery guidance\\n- `sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 `claim_task` function needs `agent_id` parameter\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `sam_claim` tool needs `agent_id` parameter in MCP schema\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 **NO SCHEMA CHANGE REQUIRED** (`Task.agent` and `Task.last_activity` already present)\\n- `tests_sam/test_cli_claim.py` and `tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 no tests for agent_id claim recording\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P1** \u2014 Multi-agent swarm dispatch is a documented first-class use case. Task abandonment creates deadlocked plans where downstream tasks block on a task that will never complete. Recovery requires manual YAML editing. The model fields already exist \u2014 this is a completion gap.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `sam_claim` MCP tool accepts optional `agent_id: str | None` parameter\\n- [ ] When `agent_id` is provided, `claim_task` writes it to `Task.agent` in the plan file at claim time\\n- [ ] When `agent_id` is provided, `claim_task` sets `Task.last_activity` to the claim timestamp (same as `started`)\\n- [ ] `sam_claim` response includes `agent` field: `{\\\"claimed\\\": true, \\\"task_id\\\": str, \\\"started\\\": str, \\\"agent\\\": str | null}`\\n- [ ] `sam_status` output for in-progress tasks surfaces `agent` and `last_activity` per task\\n- [ ] Backward compatibility: `sam_claim` without `agent_id` succeeds; `Task.agent` remains `None`\\n- [ ] New test: `sam_claim` with `agent_id=\\\"my-agent\\\"` \u2192 verify `Task.agent == \\\"my-agent\\\"` in plan file\\n- [ ] New test: `sam_claim` without `agent_id` \u2192 verify backward compat, claim succeeds, `Task.agent is None`\\n\\n**Stretch (separate issue):** `sam_claim` with `force=True` parameter allows reclaiming an `in-progress` task \u2014 guarded by staleness check (`last_activity` older than threshold).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**M (medium)** \u2014 ~3\u20135 hours. Core change is small (two function signatures, one extra write). Non-trivial: verify whether `update_status` \u2192 `update_plan_fields` composition is atomic, or whether a new atomic update path is needed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Call `sam_claim(plan=\\\"P1\\\", task=\\\"T1\\\")` \u2014 succeeds\\n2. Kill the claiming agent\\n3. Call `sam_ready(plan=\\\"P1\\\")` \u2014 T1 does not appear (status is `in-progress`)\\n4. Call `sam_status(plan=\\\"P1\\\")` \u2014 T1 shown as `in-progress` with no claiming agent, no elapsed time\\n5. No API exists to reclaim or mark T1 as abandoned\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using SAM for multi-agent swarm dispatch**, I want **`sam_claim` to record agent identity and last-activity timestamps** so that **abandoned in-progress tasks can be detected and recovered without manual file editing**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis 5 Whys\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n1. Abandoned tasks cannot be detected \u2014 no agent identity or activity timestamp on claimed tasks\\n2. `sam_claim` MCP tool accepts no `agent_id` parameter; `claim_task` has no agent parameter\\n3. `Task.agent` field exists in the model but the claim path never writes it\\n4. SAM was designed for sequential single-agent task execution; parallel/multi-agent use cases (kage-bunshin) exposed the gap\\n5. `task-worker` agent documents `sam_claim` as a prerequisite but documents no crash recovery procedure\\n\\n**Root cause:** The `Task` model already has `agent` and `last_activity` fields; the claim path and MCP API surface do not use them. This is a completion gap, not a new capability.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n1. Abandoned tasks cannot be detected \u2014 no agent identity or activity timestamp on claimed tasks\\n2. `sam_claim` MCP tool accepts no `agent_id` parameter; `claim_task` has no agent parameter\\n3. `Task.agent` field exists in the model but the claim path never writes it\\n4. SAM was designed for sequential single-agent task execution; parallel/multi-agent use cases (kage-bunshin) exposed the gap\\n5. `task-worker` agent documents `sam_claim` as a prerequisite but documents no crash recovery procedure\\n\\n**Root cause:** The `Task` model already has `agent` and `last_activity` fields; the claim path and MCP API surface do not use them. This is a completion gap, not a new capability.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**`claim_task` core change (`sam_schema/core/query.py`):**\\n\\n```python\\ndef claim_task(plan_path: Path, task_id: str, agent_id: str | None = None) -> Task:\\n    task = get_task(plan_path, task_id)\\n    if task.status != TaskStatus.NOT_STARTED:\\n        msg = f\\\"Cannot claim task '{task_id}': status is '{task.status}', expected 'not-started'.\\\"\\n        raise ValueError(msg)\\n    updated = update_status(plan_path, task_id, TaskStatus.IN_PROGRESS, timestamp_field=\\\"started\\\")\\n    if agent_id is not None:\\n        update_plan_fields(plan_path, task_id=task_id, set_fields={\\\"agent\\\": agent_id})\\n        updated = get_task(plan_path, task_id)  # re-read after second write\\n    return updated\\n```\\n\\nAlternative: extend `update_status` to accept `extra_fields: dict | None` for atomic two-field write.\\n\\n**`sam_claim` MCP tool change (`sam_schema/server.py`):**\\n\\n```python\\n@mcp.tool\\ndef sam_claim(plan: ..., task: ..., plan_dir: ... = \\\"plan\\\",\\n              agent_id: Annotated[str | None, Field(\\n                  description=\\\"Agent identity string to record on the claimed task\\\"\\n              )] = None) -> dict:\\n    ...\\n    updated_task = claim_task(plan_path, task, agent_id=agent_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"claimed\\\": True,\\n        \\\"task_id\\\": updated_task.id,\\n        \\\"started\\\": updated_task.started,\\n        \\\"agent\\\": updated_task.agent,\\n    }\\n```\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2612dd63337220dbcd8b89dcb0678ddfd3cc9a7acc4f505278f760316d3918f5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSd-Cbg\"}"}